  "hazards": [
    "The PC action config selector vector is a permutation, with 27 action-index mismatches; direct action-ID resolver indexing is invalid.",
    "The PC type-02 chain has three typed stages: AE93 config-row index, row-byte-0 package selector, then resolver-selected CE descriptor root; numeric identity at selected tail rows does not merge those namespaces.",
    "Player-command gaps 7C-7F are not free numeric values across the engine: fixed internal type-2 producers use config indices 7C, 7D, and 7F, as well as 79-7B.",
    "PC normal Attack package selection ignores AE93 and uses logical PC plus outcome-family selectors; planned action 90 is a separate namespace.",
    "Enemy Attack uses the 9853 actor/config index; AE93 selects only the zero/nonzero config branch.",
    "Item IDs DC-FF select FF in the byte-addressable tail; the loader has no local selector or FFFF guard, so the auditor excludes them before resolver access.",
    "FFFF resolver words are not selected by audited canonical sources and are not engine-rejected sentinels or free capacity.",
    "Unselected non-FFFF resolver entries are not parsed, classified as unused, or claimed free.",
    "Equal 16-bit offsets in banks CD and CE are different physical nodes.",
    "Descriptor owner-bit indices 00-0F are not logical PC identities; their runtime roles remain outside this topology census.",
    "Command 1E can leave a native package bank through a CE subscript table; direct-entry topology is not a transitive CFG.",
    "Action IDs, package selectors, battle-script opcodes, script slots, graphics selectors, and marker bytes are independent namespaces even when numeric values match."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "The census stops at bank-qualified script entrypoints and does not decode battle-animation command streams.",
    "Both descriptor masks are structural alternatives; the report does not claim that both execute simultaneously.",
    "Encoded config coverage is not runtime reachability, frequency, or story-state evidence.",
    "The command dispatcher, commands 1E/1F, and pointer-advance helper are hash-pinned only to bound the unresolved decoder problem.",
    "Auxiliary animation, graphics, effect, palette, and sound tables are outside this primary package-topology tranche.",
    "The seven pinned fixed PC type-2 producer contexts cover config indices 79, 7A, 7B, 7C, 7D, and 7F.  None of those listed contexts uses row 7E, which remains unclaimed rather than free; adjacent-width, indexed, direct-page, indirect, pointer-based, block-move, DMA, and other battle-state writes are not proved absent.",
    "Descriptor owner-bit runtime roles are not classified by this topology report."
  ],
  "nonclaims": [
    "No battle-animation opcode or operand census is complete.",
    "No CFG, call, subscript, conditional, fallthrough, lifetime, or execution-frequency proof is claimed.",
    "The encoded-operand AE93 opcode census is not a complete effective-write CFG and does not exclude adjacent-width, indexed-effective-address, direct-page, indirect, pointer-based, block-move, or DMA writes; AE92 overlap candidates are recorded without M-width claims.",
